-- title:
--   Verschiebung is injective on Fontaine's submodule L
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative ring in which the image of $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $A$ be a commutative ring carrying an $R$-bialgebra structure. Let $\pi\colon\mathcal R\to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is exactly the ideal generated by $p$. Consider the group $\mathrm{wittHom}\,R\,p\,n\,A$ of those truncated Witt vectors $x$ of length $n$ over $A$ which are primitive for the bialgebra structure, i.e. satisfy $\mathrm{map}(\Delta)(x)=\mathrm{map}(\iota_1)(x)+\mathrm{map}(\iota_2)(x)$ for the comultiplication $\Delta$ of $A$ and the two inclusions of $A$ into $A\otimes_R A$, and the group `DieudonneModule R p A` obtained as the direct limit of these groups along the shift maps. Let $z$ be an element of this direct limit which lies in `fontaineHodge R p π`, that is, $z$ is the image of some primitive $x$ of some length $n$ whose underlying truncated Witt vector belongs to `fontaineKer p n π`, and suppose that the endomorphism `verschiebung` of the direct limit, induced levelwise by the Verschiebung of truncated Witt vectors, annihilates $z$. Then $z=0$.
--
--   This is assertion (iii) of Fontaine's theorem on finite commutative group schemes over Witt vectors: the injectivity of $V$ on the submodule $L$, one of the axioms for the pair $(L,M)$ to form a Honda system. It is used in the construction of the Honda system attached to such a group scheme, namely by [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge).
